Genuine picohttpparser, unmodified picohttpparser.c and picohttpparser.h.
Upstream https://github.com/h2o/picohttpparser
Revision dd573d8fa9264c646a400e96ce9f07dea6f156e4
Copyright Kazuho Oku, Tokuhiro Matsuno, Daisuke Murase, Shigeo Mitsunari.
Clarice uses the MIT option; full licence is at the top of both source files.

The response parser and streaming chunk decoder are linked with section garbage
collection; request parsing is not used. Target builds use NDEBUG to omit the
unreachable corrupt-decoder-state assertion (not malformed-input checks).
Host sanitizer tests keep assertions enabled. No SSE on the 68000 target.
../../http-response.inc contains policy and native input/allocation adaptation.
Headers grow from 512 to at most 8192 bytes, preserving the previous wire bound.
Header descriptors are sized from the received lines and freed before file I/O.
No permanent Core state or custom duplicate HTTP/chunk grammar.
HTTP policy remains strict CRLF, status 200, identity content encoding, exactly
one unambiguous Content-Length or HTTP/1.1 chunked Transfer-Encoding. No redirects,
TLS, EOF-delimited bodies or interim responses in this contained batch.
